## Problem classes

### `Dead proxy after crash`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Browser hangs on all HTTP | Global still points at old port | `onDestroy`/`onTaskRemoved` disable; boot/start clear if not PROXY |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `SecurityException on putString`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Proxy "on" in UI but Global unchanged | No `WRITE_SECURE_SETTINGS` | Shizuku or ADB grant; listen still; UI "system proxy inactive" |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `Stale loopback saved as user proxy`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| PROXY→VPN leaves `http_proxy=127.0.0.1:oldPort` | `enable()` saved leftover `127.0.0.1:oldPort` (previous session) as "user proxy"; `disable()` restored it | Never save/restore `127.0.0.1:*`. `isLoopbackProxy` any port → treat as ours → restore `:0` |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `hasPermission false positive`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| `hasPermission()` true but `enable()` throws `SecurityException` | `Settings.Global.getString` does not throw without grant; archive try/catch on read always passed | `hasPermission`: no-op `putString(HTTP_PROXY, current)` round-trip; catch `SecurityException` |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `HTTP_PROXY stuck after global OFF`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| User toggles OFF; apps hang on HTTP; `settings get global http_proxy` still `127.0.0.1:port` until proxy service finally tears down (or forever if wedged) | Global clear only ran inside service teardown behind a mutex blocked by a hung native wait | Clear Global **first** on OFF/swap (`ConnectionOrchestrator.applyOff` / `stopProxyStack`) and on ACTION_STOP (`disableBlocking()` before mutex). Idempotent double-disable is fine |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-09 -->

### `Captive portal while PROXY starting`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Kindle/Fire OS shows no internet; `tabletcaptiveportal.com` 502; Wi-Fi never validates; ZT node may still be ONLINE | Global `HTTP_PROXY` set **before** uplink resolve can return public names (netd timeout / `no uplink` on unvalidated Wi-Fi). Captive HTTP then goes through us → empty resolve → 502. Chicken-egg: VALIDATED never comes while we intercept | **Listen** on 127.0.0.1 before NODE_UP (T16). **Default:** defer `enable()` until public-name probe returns addresses — captive checks stay direct. **Skip-probe** (Settings / AUTO per PROXY link): enable at listen for air-gap. Sticky. Node retry must not stop listen or `disable()` while PROXY wanted. Kick on `onAvailable` / INTERNET — **not** `NET_CAPABILITY_VALIDATED` as enable trigger |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-09 -->

### `Global proxy enabled but all HTTP 502`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Every CONNECT 502; logs `dns FAIL via=netd timeout` or `ENONET`; `ztDomains=-`; overlay join OK | Apps honor Global; we must resolve then TCP. Health check is **CONNECT to a probe host**, not DNS-through-HTTP. Netd on `activeNetwork` ENONET while unvalidated Wi-Fi sits in `allNetworks`. Empty Settings fallbacks → UDP loop is a no-op | **Heal** (WAN default): scan non-VPN `allNetworks` (Wi-Fi vs cell preference), netd then UDP to that net’s DHCP DNS, `bindSocket` uplink TCP. User fallback IPs still after that. Do **not** un-stick Global on probe fail. OFF/swap: `disable()` first (T16) |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-09 -->

### `Un-stick Global on failed DNS probe`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Air-gapped / WAN-DNS-down overlay HTTP via system proxy dies; or `http_proxy` chatters `127.0.0.1:port` ↔ `:0` | Public-name probe (`example.com`) used as liveness for Global. Overlay IPs never needed that probe. Consecutive fails + capability `onAvailable` aborting backoff makes 2 fails / 2 oks sub-second | Keep Global sticky after enable. Air-gap: skip-probe opt-in. Heal public DNS separately. Never `disable()` from Doze pause |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-09 -->

### `Stale adb forward empty reply`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| `curl: (52) Empty reply from server` in ~2ms through `adb forward` | Proxy rebound a new ephemeral port on restart; adbd accepts the forward then fails to connect, which reads as an instant empty reply | Re-read `adb shell settings get global http_proxy` and re-forward the current port. Boundary: a **10s hang → 502** is ZT-side (see libzt rules), not staleness |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `CONNECT relay stagnation`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Apps (TikTok search, Chrome, …) get slower/stuttery the longer PROXY stays up; restarting the proxy makes them snappy again. Some features “fail” then work after leaving the app. | CONNECT tunnels (HTTP/2 keep-alives) never idle-out. Each holds **2** `zt-relay` threads + **1** `Dispatchers.IO` thread. Old **fixed 64** pool deadlocks at **32** concurrent CONNECTs (both pumps queued, neither runs). System DNS also 6s-NXDOMAIN then negative-cache bursts (`Unable to resolve host …: No address associated with hostname`) — leave-app / retry recovers. | Cached relay pool (`newCachedThreadPool`) + **60s shared idle** timeout (`ProxyRelay`). Java sockets poll every 5s and check last-byte either direction. ZeroTierInputStream maps `SO_RCVTIMEO` to EOF — do **not** use the 5s poll on ZT; set ZT recv timeout to the idle window. Watch: if 60s is too aggressive (video pause / HTTP/2 PING slower than 60s), raise `DEFAULT_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS`. DNS 6s NXDOMAIN is **not** fixed here. |

